{"name":"Tennis Ball","hex":"#dfff4f","fetched":"2026-10-13","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"tennis ball","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A hollow, bouncy rubber ball, pressurized and covered with usually yellow felt, used in the game of tennis."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/tennis_ball"}],"entries":[{"title":"Tennis ball","blocks":[{"text":"A tennis ball is a small, hollow ball used in games of tennis and real tennis. Tennis balls are fluorescent yellow in professional competitions, but in recreational play other colors are also used. Tennis balls are covered in a fibrous felt, which modifies their aerodynamic properties, and each has a white curvilinear oval covering it."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/41/Closeup_of_a_tennis_ball_%282%29.jpg/330px-Closeup_of_a_tennis_ball_%282%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Tennis_ball"},{"title":"Tennis","blocks":[{"text":"Tennis is a racket sport that is played either individually against a single opponent (singles) or between two teams of two players each (doubles). Each player uses a tennis racket strung with a cord to strike a hollow rubber ball covered with felt over or around a net and into the opponent's court. The objective is to manoeuvre the ball in such a way that the opponent is not able to play a valid return. If a player is unable to return the ball successfully, the opponent scores a point."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/94/2013_Australian_Open_-_Guillaume_Rufin.jpg/330px-2013_Australian_Open_-_Guillaume_Rufin.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Tennis"},{"title":"Ball","blocks":[{"text":"A ball is a round object. Balls can have several uses. For example they are used in ball games, where the play of the game follows the state of the ball as it is hit, kicked or thrown by players. Balls can also be used for simpler activities, such as catch or juggling. Balls made from hard-wearing materials are used in engineering applications to provide very low friction bearings, known as ball bearings. Black-powder weapons use stone and metal balls as projectiles."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/ce/Many_balls.jpg/330px-Many_balls.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ball"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/c3/Cmglee_tennis_ball_interior.jpg/500px-Cmglee_tennis_ball_interior.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/c3/Cmglee_tennis_ball_interior.jpg/1280px-Cmglee_tennis_ball_interior.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/c3/Cmglee_tennis_ball_interior.jpg/500px-Cmglee_tennis_ball_interior.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"A tennis ball sliced open to show its rubber bladder","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ACmglee_tennis_ball_interior.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/0d/Tennis_ball_blanks_and_felt.jpg/500px-Tennis_ball_blanks_and_felt.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/0d/Tennis_ball_blanks_and_felt.jpg/1280px-Tennis_ball_blanks_and_felt.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/0d/Tennis_ball_blanks_and_felt.jpg/500px-Tennis_ball_blanks_and_felt.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Tennis balls and internal \"blanks\" manufactured by Dunlop Slazenger","link":"https://